# Git Branch Workflow

Multiple agents work in parallel on this repo. Never commit or push directly to `main`.

## Before any commit

1. Check current branch: `git branch --show-current`
2. If on `main`, create and switch to a topic branch first:
   ```bash
   git checkout -b <type>/<short-description>
   # e.g. fix/chat-mobile-overflow, feat/blog-tags, chore/deps-update
   ```

## Branch naming

`<type>/<kebab-description>` — keep it under 40 chars.
Types: `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `refactor`, `docs`.

## Committing

- Stage only files relevant to the current task.
- Commit on the topic branch, then push with `-u`:
  ```bash
  git push -u origin HEAD
  ```

## Never

- `git push origin main` (direct push to main)
- `git commit` while on `main`
- Force-push without explicit user request
- Delete `dev` or `main` branches (local or remote)
- Delete Supabase `dev` or `main` branches/environments (including via MCP/CLI/dashboard actions)
